blank\">this template</a>:</p>\n<ol>\n<li>\n<p><strong>Column 1</strong>: High Density</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><strong>Column 2</strong>: Low Density</p>\n</li>\n</ol>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Complete an LR section<span class=\"cursor-pointer \n                      cursor-help underline decoration-dotted underline-offset-2\n                    \" data-state=\"closed\">*</span> using any workout, but with one small adjustment: Write your Mission in either the High-Density or&nbsp;Low-Density column in the spreadsheet.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Choose which column to place your Mission into based on how information-dense your Mission is.</p>\n<ol>\n<li>\n<p>The High Density column is where you write your high information density Missions.</p>\n<ol>\n<li>\n<p>A Mission with high information density will use words and concepts from the stimulus directly without referential phrasing, glazing over the&nbsp;details, and characterizing information (\"all that stuff\") to avoid having to say it directly.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><strong>Example Mission in the High-Density Bucket</strong>: Whether there actually is more food in the ocean tropics versus the freshwater tropics</p>\n</li>\n</ol>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>The Low Density column is where you write your low information density Missions.</p>\n<ol>\n<li>\n<p>A Mission with low information density will use referential phrasing (\"this,\" \"that,\" \"it,\" \"they,\" \"the conclusion,\" etc.) to gloss over the direct words and concepts from the stimulus,  omit the&nbsp;details like specific nouns and verbs, and group information together with broad characterizations (\"good things\").</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><strong>Example Mission on the Same Question in the Low-Density Bucket</strong>: Food is important</p>\n</li>\n</ol>\n</li>\n</ol>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>After you complete the section, review the spreadsheet to note which questions produced Low-Density Missions.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Return to the questions that produced Low-Density Missions the next day and try to make a new higher density Mission before you Camo the section.</p>\n</li>\n</ol></div><div class=\"pt-2\"><a href=\"/workouts-and-routines/workouts/density-buckets\"><button class=\"\n    inline-flex cursor-pointer items-center justify-center rounded-full\n    font-extrabold uppercase lh-outline\n    [transition:background-color_0.15s_cubic-bezier(0.4,0,0.2,1),border-color_0.15s_cubic-bezier(0.4,0,0.2,1),box-shadow_0.15s_cubic-bezier(0.4,0,0.2,1),translate_0.15s_cubic-bezier(0.4,0,0.2,1)]\n    disabled:cursor-not-allowed disabled:opacity-50\n   \n          border-black text-black\n          hover:not-disabled:-translate-x-[3px]\n          hover:not-disabled:-translate-y-[3px]\n          hover:not-disabled:shadow-[3px_3px_0_0_#171712]\n          active:not-disabled:-translate-x-[1px]\n          active:not-disabled:-translate-y-[1px]\n          active:not-disabled:shadow-[1px_1px_0_0_#171712]\n         h-[38px] gap-2 text-caption-medium border-[2px] pl-4 pr-3\">See full workout details<span class=\"flex items-center justify-center\"><svg width=\"15\" height=\"12\" class=\"\" viewBox=\"0 0 26 19\" fill=\"none\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" data-testid=\"arrow-icon\"><path d=\"M20.25 10.9383H1.66667C1.19444 10.9383 0.798611 10.7786 0.479167 10.4592C0.159722 10.1397 0 9.74389 0 9.27167C0 8.79945 0.159722 8.40361 0.479167 8.08417C0.798611 7.76472 1.19444 7.605 1.66667 7.605H20.25L15.5 2.855C15.1667 2.52167 15.0069 2.13278 15.0208 1.68833C15.0347 1.24389 15.1944 0.855 15.5 0.521667C15.8333 0.188333 16.2292 0.0147222 16.6875 0.000833333C17.1458 -0.0130556 17.5417 0.146667 17.875 0.48L25.5 8.105C25.6667 8.27167 25.7847 8.45222 25.8542 8.64667C25.9236 8.84111 25.9583 9.04945 25.9583 9.27167C25.9583 9.49389 25.9236 9.70222 25.8542 9.89667C25.7847 10.0911 25.6667 10.2717 25.5 10.4383L17.875 18.0633C17.5417 18.3967 17.1458 18.5564 16.6875 18.5425C16.2292 18.5286 15.8333 18.355 15.5 18.0217C15.1944 17.6883 15.0347 17.2994 15.0208 16.855C15.0069 16.4106 15.1